Error [E-ERR-SUFFIX]: `Error!` is a retired suffix failure contract.
  --> tests/ui/try_suffix_staged.jet:5:18
    |
  5 | fn compute() Int E! -> Ok(1)
    |                  ^^
 Why: Jet puts the error contract before its type so the success role and error role stay distinct in every type position.
 Fix: Write `!Error`, or write `?Success !Error` when the success can be absent.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E-ERR-SUFFIX

Error [E-ERR-PROPAGATE]: Bare `?` propagation is retired.
  --> tests/ui/try_suffix_staged.jet:8:19
    |
  8 |     x :: compute()?
    |                   ^
 Why: Fallible calls propagate automatically; `?(text)` is reserved for adding one failure-context frame.
 Fix: Remove the trailing `?`, or write `?(text)` to add one context frame.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E-ERR-PROPAGATE
